Noticed while verifying the class_namespaces fix in expand_class (karr #11 follow-up).

IO::K8s::Role::Resource::_k8s_attr_info does an exact-class lookup:

    return $IO::K8s::Resource::_attr_registry{$class} // {};

No @ISA walk. So a consumer class registered via class_namespaces that merely
subclasses a shipped class:

    package My::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Pod;
    use parent \x27IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Pod\x27;

resolves correctly through expand_class now, but _inflate_struct() sees an empty
attribute registry for it: every nested field is passed through raw, and the
first typed attribute (metadata) fails its type constraint.

Workaround today is to re-declare the attributes with the k8s DSL in the
subclass, which works and is what the POD example implies -- but nothing says so,
and "subclass a shipped class to add a helper method" is the obvious reading of
the class_namespaces feature.

Decide between:
  (a) make _k8s_attr_info walk @ISA and merge (nearest wins),
  (b) document that a class_namespaces class must declare its own k8s attributes.

(a) is the smaller surprise but touches the hot inflate path for every attribute
lookup, so it wants a cache. Pre-existing, not a regression.
Resolved in 83d066a (option a, confirmed with user). _k8s_attr_info + _k8s_attributes walk @ISA: nearest-wins info merge, deduplicated attribute union, per-class caches invalidated (direct + descendant sweep) on k8s registration. t/46_class_namespaces_inflate.t: 5 subtests, 4 red pre-fix (inflate collapsed metadata, TO_JSON empty, missing inherited attrs), full suite PASS (49 files, 3920 tests). Drift noted for follow-up: (1) APIObject::api_version derives wire version only for IO::K8s::Api/*/ApiextensionsApiserver/KubeAggregator namespaces - a class_namespaces subclass returns undef and TO_JSON omits apiVersion (test subclass declares sub api_version); (2) Moo MI constructor aggregates only first @ISA chain (documented in test, not our bug); (3) compare_to_schema still reads registry directly.
